    "text": "<@UK3LH8CF5> I'm the one who listens to podcasts and video 2.6x, which should help explain (or be explained by) my normal speech speed. :wolf: A few things I will listen to slower: actual narrative, like radio shows, go faster.  3blue1brown or something similarly dense.  Typical NPR will be sped up further because they talk so slowly.  And the other trick is that I pause stuff all the time when thinking is required.",
